       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg for adults. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify a dose that high. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock, because amlodipine has a long half-life.\n\n- **Typical dosing:** The usual start is 2.5\u20135 mg by mouth once daily. It can be titrated to a maximum of 10 mg once daily.\n- **If 5 mg was meant:** I can enter 5 mg PO daily right away.\n- **If 10 mg was meant:** I can enter 10 mg PO daily.\n- **If more blood pressure control is needed:** Adding a second agent from a different class is usually the next step. Examples are an ACE inhibitor or ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic. Pharmacy or the attending can help choose.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
